WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.135
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.469
We're here with John Oliver.
Very exciting.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.438
We are going to be spending
New Year's Eve together.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:06.606
-Yeah we are.
We're going to be doing

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.674
stand-up in Las Vegas.
-Yeah, we are.

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:10.143
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.844
-And you've noticed
that it's very funny,

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.446
the room they have us
doing stand-up in.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.982
-Yes, because
it's Adele's theater.

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.516
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:21.688
And so for one night only Adele
ain't going to be there.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.556
And I hope that's made
very clear

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.392
to the people that turn up
to that theater.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.628
-And it's just you and Adele
are this Venn diagram

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.697
where just a tiny slice
of British...

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:34.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.402
That's it. Just like...
-That's it. That's it.

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:39.138
That's it.

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:40.473
-I'm fascinated.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.874
I mean, you do New Year's Eve
shows every year.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.342
-Yeah, I love it.
-And you've always said

00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:45.512
it's the best way to spend New
Year's, and you've been kind.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.079
-Yeah, because you're not
really spending it.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.782
You're kind of basically
doing something else instead.

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.251
It's classic
displacement activity, right?

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.519
-Yeah.
-So I love it.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:56.022
I hate New Year's
as an evening, I hate it.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.024
And so now I do stand-up,
which I love,

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.160
and they cancel each other out.
It's great.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.527
-I'm very excited to be
doing it with you.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.295
Our friend Brooks Wheelan
will be there as well.

00:01:03.295 --> 00:01:04.497
-Yes, he's going to be there.
-Literally

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.932
the greatest person
to be on the road with.

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.066
You're on the road with him
all the time.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.734
-Yeah. He's the absolute
greatest, funniest,

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:11.303
nicest, fantastic human being.
-Where do you think

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:12.405
we'll be at midnight?

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.507
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:18.277
I mean, listen,
the high-percentage guess

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.613
is back in our rooms alone.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:21.815
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.148
-But having --
-That's what the money --

00:01:23.148 --> 00:01:25.518
That's what house money is on.
-House money is saying

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.320
having a nice, quiet night,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.887
getting extra sleep
and getting an early flight

00:01:28.887 --> 00:01:31.091
out back to our families.
I will say, having said that,

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.259
the tradition of coming
on this show

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:37.497
and things turning out other
than I might otherwise imagine,

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.165
there is a chance you're going
to be able to cut from this

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.600
that it's just you and me
in our underwear,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.236
just running down the Strip,
unloading firearms in the air.

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.505
-Yeah.
-We're golden gods!

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.940
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.643
2024 is going to be great!
Pow pow!

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.712
-Pow pow! To the sphere!

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:56.449
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.985
-Where's Bono?
-Yeah!

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.385
-We find him.
-We find --

00:02:00.385 --> 00:02:02.388
-We got to find Bono.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.857
-There's nothing worse
than an English person saying,

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:07.360
"Where's Bono?" with a gun
in his hand as well.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.595
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:12.965
"Bring me an Irishman!"
Yeah.

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:16.803
-You and I, we were --
we podcasted together.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.171
-Yeah.
-Strike Force Five,

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.172
which I heard
very nice things about.

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:21.273
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:25.745
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.513
-I didn't know if it would work
when we first started doing it.

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:29.682
-I was almost sure it wouldn't.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.884
-So, yeah, it's a very,
very pleasant surprise

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.454
that it turned out okay.
People seem to like it.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:35.988
Even if I did wonder
that some people

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:38.725
were listening with
a pathological interest.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:41.527
"Oh, wow. Let's just see
what these five lab rats do

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.595
when they talk to each other."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.595 --> 00:02:44.930
-Or talk over each other.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.765
-That's right. Absolutely.
In many, many ways.

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:49.635
-My favorite thing
about the podcast was,

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.104
and I should say
we should both shout out.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.672
We've talked about it a lot.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.173
Jimmy Fallon
hosted episode five.

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.641
-It's a masterpiece.
-It's a masterpiece.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:58.244
It's genuinely --
-I'm so grateful to him.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.147
I am so grateful to him
for what he gave us.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:03.816
I needed those laughs
so much at that point

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:07.352
and only he could provide it.
It's just perfect.

00:03:07.352 --> 00:03:10.289
-It was a very poorly run

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:13.058
and yet, because of that
exceptionally funny,

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:15.728
basically "Newlywed Game"
where Fallon texted our wives.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.364
But we did find out super-fun
things about our wives,

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.601
including the angriest you
ever were with your wife

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.569
was when you went
to a pirate party.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.437
-Yeah.
-Pirate-themed party.

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:28.174
-Yeah, because I dressed
like a pirate.

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.910
-Yeah.
-And we were there first.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.613
And I remember
the host of the party

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.815
not really being dressed
like a pirate and thinking,

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.383
"oh, that's a shame,

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.152
but at least there's lots of
pirates coming."

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:41.821
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.222
Then...

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:46.659
Then another couple turn up.
Very much not pirate-based,

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.928
and I'm getting a sinking
feeling in my stomach

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:51.864
saying, "The third one
will be the key here."

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.200
Not dressed like a pirate.
And I really was dressed,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.235
like, very much like a pirate.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:59.505
-Yeah.
-So I spent a pretty angry

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:03.042
afternoon and evening dressed
like a pirate among non-pirates.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.376
-Now, I also want to stress.

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:06.578
I want to say even if everybody
dressed like a pirate...

00:04:06.578 --> 00:04:08.113
-Yes.
-...I'm going to go out

00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:09.748
on a limb and say you would
have hated that.

00:04:09.748 --> 00:04:10.917
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.453
-Oh, the evening was not
going to go great for me,

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:19.625
but at least I wanted to be able
to be among other pirates,

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:21.194
and I really wasn't.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.796
I was among people dressed
in kind of casual way.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.764
-And this is a photo
of you and your wife.

00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:27.866
And I do want to note
she's having a grand old time,

00:04:27.866 --> 00:04:31.971
and you are the unhappiest
I've ever seen a pirate.

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.172
-Now, you say that.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.473
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:35.674
You say that.

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:37.810
I would say...
[ Laughs ]

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.213
I would say
a pirate on a pirate ship

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:42.582
would look that unhappy

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.684
if none of the other pirates
were dressed like pirates.

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.986
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:50.256
-If it was like Casual Friday
on Pirates of the Caribbean.

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:52.691
-That's right. Exactly.
You go, "Hey, guys.

00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:56.462
Guys, you have to let me know.
I've pirated up over here.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:59.265
You can't hang me out
to dry like this. Arrr."

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.599
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.599 --> 00:05:02.902
-Also an eyepatch
is even funnier

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:04.303
when the pirate's
wearing glasses.

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:08.908
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.876
-That is such a --

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:13.312
And if you're wondering, is
an eyepatch more comfortable

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:15.047
over the glasses
or under the glasses?

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:17.517
It's a coin flip.
You just have to rotate.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:18.518
Neither is good.

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:20.152
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:21.587
-Well, God love Kate.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:24.523
Also, it does feel like Kate's
goatee is also an eye patch.

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:26.825
-Yes. That's right.

00:05:26.825 --> 00:05:28.861
-It does feel like you guys
bought a thing of iPads

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.163
and you're like,
"We got to use them all."

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.363
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.363 --> 00:05:33.966
Whether it makes sense or not.
-That's right.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.868
Yeah. That's right.
Also, I just think

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.937
she could get away
with it more than me.

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.571
I don't know if it's the belt.

00:05:39.571 --> 00:05:41.073
If it's the Pirates
of the Caribbean.

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:43.676
-Oh, everybody who's
seen this photo thinks that.

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.145
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.413
You're like,
"Also, I'm going to say

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.949
something you guys
might not have clocked.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:52.618
Kate makes a great pirate."
Yeah. No. We're there.

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:53.986
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:55.655
I can't wait for
New Year's Eve, buddy,

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:56.689
and hopefully
I'll see you before that.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.024
-I know. I never
thought I'd say that.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.058
-Yeah. No kidding.
John Oliver, everybody.

00:06:00.058 --> 00:06:02.895
"Last Week Tonight"
Sundays on HBO, streams on Max.

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:05.531
We'll be right back with
Aaron Jackson and Josh Sharp.

